ator state and environment before planning a MiniPlayer component that reads song, artist, cover, and playback state from storage props and displays only when a current song exists and playback isn't stopped.\n\nSince isplaying briefly flips false during song switches, I'll introduce a new `player-hasSong` storage key set true only after successful playback starts and false on stop, so the mini bar stays visible through that transition without altering baseline logic. I'm laying out the mini player as a row with a clickable cover image, title/artist column, time display, and a play/pause button, with the whole row opening the play page on tap.\n\nFor click handling, child components like the button naturally win gesture competition over the parent row's onClick, so tapping the button won't trigger navigation. For opening the play page itself, I'm designing a guarded helper that checks the router's current state name and a navigating flag before calling pushUrl via getUIContext().getRouter(), resetting the flag once the transition completes to avoid duplicate navigations from rapid taps.\n\nNow I'm setting up the PlayPage itself, registering it in main_pages.json and building the root column with safe-area padding, plus a top row containing a back button that rotates the back arrow icon to point downward for the collapse gesture.\n\nCurrent time and duration labels, play/pause button swaps between ids depending on state. For back handling I'm adding an `isClosing` guard flag so rapid taps on the down arrow during the exit transition don't trigger multiple pops, and onBackPress checks that flag to consume the event. I'm also considering the edge case of opening PlayPage with no active song.\n\nFor seeking, I'm implementing an `AudioPlayUtils.seek(ms)` helper that updates stored player time and calls the player's seek method. Since AVPlayer's default seek mode snaps to the previous sync frame, I'm worried about stale timeUpdate callbacks firing before seek completes and causing a visible jump back, so I'm planning to track a `seekingTarget` value to filter out those stale updates.\n\nI'm weighing whether to register directly on AVPlayer's native 'seekDone' event versus just tracking a time window after seek and ignoring timeUpdate values that deviate too much from the target, since the player instance gets recreated on release and re-registering listeners per seek adds complexity.\n\n","startTime":1792379404607,"lastModifiedTime":1792379427502},{"id":"toolu_bdrk_01S5JyuyiBGVuQkYpCSi1zVR","type":"TOOL","toolName":"run_command","params":{"command":"export PATH=/Applications/DevEco-Studio.app/Contents/sdk/default/openharmony/toolchains:$PATH; hdc list targets; docker ps --format '{{.Names}} {{.Image}} {{.Ports}}' 2>&1; ls ../common/.venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages | grep -i hypium; ls logs/baseline | head -50","description":"Check device, docker API container, hypium install","prefix_rule":"[\"hdc\",\"list\"]","working_directory":"/Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/cmu-spec102"},"toolState":"executed","result":{"output":"Command executed successfully.\nExit code: 0\nOutput:\n127.0.0.1:5555\nnetease_cloud_music_api binaryify/netease_cloud_music_api 0.0.0.0:3000->3000/tcp, [::]:3000->3000/tcp\nhypium\nhypium-6.1.0.210.dist-info\nb01-index.jpeg\nb01-index.json\nb02-search.jpeg\nb02-search.json\nb03-sheet.jpeg\nb03-sheet.json\nb04-after-play.jpeg\nb04-after-play.json\nb05-popup.jpeg\nb05-popup.json\nb06-popup-later.json\nb07-paused.jpeg\nb07-paused.json\nb08-index-after.jpeg\nb08-index-after.json\nb09-menu.jpeg\nb09-menu.json\nb10-settings.jpeg\nb10-settings.json\nb11-before-restart.json\nb12-after-restart.json\nv1-settings.json\nv2-settings-after-restart.json\n","metadata":{"cwd":"/Users/bress/Documents/code/harmonycup-work/cmu-spec102","autoRun":true,"state":"completed","runMode":"yolo","taskId":"6ft5v6","output":"127.0.0.1:5555\nnetease_cloud_music_api binaryify/netease_cloud_music_api 0.0.0.0:3000->3000/tcp, [::]:3000->30